 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 4,
   "y": 6,
   "text": "THE BOAT HALL. A sixareen, a six-oared fishing boat of the type that went out to the far haaf fishing, forty miles into the Atlantic, in open boats. The men were out a day or more at a time in open boats. The Norse lines of the hull have changed very little in a thousand years."
  },
  {
   "x": 10,
   "y": 6,
   "text": "THE PICTISH STONES. Carved around 1,300 years ago by the Picts, who lived here before the Norse arrived. A mirror, a comb, a serpent, a crescent. No-one is quite sure what the symbols mean, but they are very stylish about it."
  }
 ],
